     2	
     3	// Photo machine capture, ticket 01 — ranking the catalog against a photographed
     4	// name plate. Pure: no UI, no SwiftData, no Vision.
     5	//
     6	// The job is not "find the best row" — it is "be right, or say you are not
     7	// sure". D23 keys history, prefill and PRs on the model UUID, so a confident
     8	// wrong match splits the user's own training history exactly the way duplicate
     9	// catalog identities did (codex-review-4). Hence D33: this file proposes, the
    10	// user confirms, and a weak or ambiguous best answer is reported as such.
    11	//
    12	// The first cross-review of this file (`.scratch/photo-machine-capture/
    13	// codex-review.md`) found four ways to score a *confident wrong row*, and the
    14	// shape below is what closes them:
    15	//
    16	//  - evidence the plate offers but a row cannot explain counts against that row,
    17	//    including words the catalog has never seen ("NEWCO");
    18	//  - a row whose manufacturer the plate contradicts cannot be preselected;
    19	//  - a near-tie is an ambiguity to surface, never a winner to pick;
    20	//  - one recognised word cannot stand in as evidence for two different catalog
    21	//    words ("abduction" is not "adduction").
    22	
    23	/// One ranked catalog row.
    24	struct CatalogMatch: Equatable {
    25	    let modelID: UUID
    26	    let manufacturer: String
    27	    let modelName: String
