codex
The corpus sweep found a regression serious enough to determine the verdict: even with a pristine full manufacturer-and-model reading, four seeded rows preselect the wrong UUID. Dropping lone letters only on the photo side makes `D.Y.`, `T-`, and the word `a` disappear while those high-IDF tokens remain in candidate denominators; generic sibling rows then win. I’m validating the build/tests and documenting exact scores plus the remaining UI/state issues.
